    "title": "CB One Rudolf 260",
    "descriptionHtml": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span>The Rudolph is a floating plug based on the Ryan, which overcomes the drawbacks of a larger body. The larger body also increases the amplitude of the action, but the design minimizes the amplitude, resulting in a swift, agile action that moves quickly over short distances. The slender shape minimizes lateral movement, resulting in light drag and reducing the physical strain of operating a big plug. It can accommodate a wide range of hook weights, and a major advantage is that it allows the use of lighter hooks that penetrate well, especially when targeting yellowtail amberjack. Of course, when targeting large tuna, use thicker, stronger hooks.</span></p><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span>Length 260 </span> mm</p></li><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Gr.175</p></li><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><span>Color Mahi Mahi</span></p></li></ul>",
